---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="AI Opportunity & Cost Review Services | Cloud & Capital" description="Work with Diana Molski to identify practical AI opportunities for your business and understand AI and cloud spending.">
  <main id="main-content" class="services">
    <section class="intro shell" aria-labelledby="services-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Work with Cloud &amp; Capital</p>
      <h1 id="services-title">Make technology work<br/><em>for your business.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">Find practical ways to use AI—and understand what your AI and cloud services are costing.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="mailto:diana@cloudandcapital.com?subject=Cost%20review%20inquiry">Tell me about your business <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="download" href="/downloads/cloud-and-capital-services-overview.pdf" download>Download the one-page overview</a></div>
    </section>

    <section class="fit shell" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">A good fit</p>
      <h2 id="fit-title">A useful starting point for your next technology decision.</h2>
      <p>You run a small business and want useful ways to start using AI. Or your business has meaningful AI or cloud spending, a rising bill, or an unclear cost decision.</p>
      <p>Referral partners: introduce me to the business owner or the person responsible for the budget or workflow. We can start with a conversation about their question and available data.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="offers shell" aria-label="Review services">
      <article><p class="eyebrow">01 · AI opportunity review</p><h2>Where could AI help your business?</h2><p>Discuss repetitive tasks, current tools, and everyday bottlenecks. Identify a few workflows where AI could help, considering human review, sensitive information, and likely tool costs.</p><p>Start with one process: drafting routine replies, preparing a first draft of a document, or organizing information for someone to check. The right idea depends on the work and the information involved.</p><p class="takeaway">Receive prioritized ideas and one proposed pilot, with a simple way to check whether it helps. Building or integrating that pilot is a separate scope.</p></article>
      <article><p class="eyebrow">02 · AI &amp; cloud cost review</p><h2>What is driving the bill—and what needs attention?</h2><p>Review supplied bills and usage exports to explain cost drivers and allocation gaps. Assess opportunities such as model selection, caching, batch processing, and cloud usage where the evidence supports them.</p><p>Where checked outcomes exist, compare cost per usable result, including retries and rework. Your team defines and checks what counts as usable; billing data alone cannot establish output quality.</p><p class="takeaway">Receive a spending summary, prioritized findings, and recommended next steps with assumptions and dependencies. Operational changes are validated with your team.</p></article>
    </section>

    <section class="process shell" aria-labelledby="process-title"><p class="eyebrow">A practical starting point</p><h2 id="process-title">Start small. Get a clear next step.</h2><div class="steps"><div><h3>Define the question</h3><p>Choose one business workflow or one area of spending. Agree the available information, scope, deliverables, and fee before work begins.</p></div><div><h3>Review the evidence</h3><p>Review your process or supplied cost records alongside the business context. Make gaps and assumptions visible.</p></div><div><h3>Decide what to do</h3><p>Walk through the findings and priorities. Implementation and ongoing support are scoped separately.</p></div></div></section>

    <section class="about-review shell" aria-labelledby="reviewer-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">Your reviewer</p><h2 id="reviewer-title">Hi, I’m Diana.</h2><p>I bring a finance background and FinOps training to the questions behind technology spending. I built <a href="https://lens.cloudandcapital.com">AI Cost Lens</a> and <a href="https://guard.cloudandcapital.com">Cloud Cost Guard</a> to make cost evidence easier to understand.</p><p class="credentials">B.S. Business Administration, Finance · FinOps Certified Practitioner · FinOps Certified FOCUS Analyst · AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner</p><p class="credentials">Interested in investing basics? Explore my <a href="/#writing">educational writing</a>.</p></div><aside><h3>Have a workflow, bill, or decision you need another set of eyes on?</h3><p>Tell me what you are working on and what you want to improve or understand.</p><a href="mailto:diana@cloudandcapital.com">diana@cloudandcapital.com →</a></aside></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .services { padding: 9rem 0 5rem; color: #242b28; }
  .shell { width: min(calc(100% - 4rem), 72rem); margin-inline: auto; }
  .eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-ui); font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: .13em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #4d6e63; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  h1,h2,h3 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.14; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 6vw, 5.4rem); letter-spacing: -.045em; }
  h1 em { color: #4d6e63; font-weight: 400; }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.5rem); margin-bottom: 1.3rem; }
  h3 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: .9rem; }
  p { font-family: var(--font-ui); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .lede { max-width: 43rem; font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 1.7rem; }
  .actions { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:1.7rem; flex-wrap:wrap; margin: 2rem 0 4rem; }
  .button { padding: 1rem 1.4rem; background:#4d6e63; color:white; font-family:var(--font-ui); text-decoration:none; border-radius:3px; }
  .download, a { color:#36594c; text-underline-offset: .25em; }
  a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #36594c; outline-offset:5px; }
  .fit { background: #e1e8df; padding: 2.3rem 2.6rem; }
  .fit h2 { max-width: 45rem; }
  .fit p { max-width: 58rem; }
  .offers { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:4rem; padding-block:4rem; }
  .offers article { min-width:0; }
  .takeaway { color:#36594c; border-left:3px solid #b78678; padding-left:1.2rem; margin-top:1.6rem; }
  .process { padding-block:3rem; border-block:1px solid #c9d1c8; }
  .steps { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:2.7rem; margin-top:2rem; }
  .about-review { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr; gap:4rem; padding-top:4rem; }
  .credentials { font-size:.88rem; color:#505a54; }
  aside { background:#4d6e63; color:white; padding:2.3rem; }
  aside a { color:white; font-family:var(--font-ui); overflow-wrap:anywhere; }
  @media(max-width:760px) { .services {padding-top:7rem;} .shell {width:calc(100% - 2.5rem);} .fit {padding:1.6rem;} .offers,.steps,.about-review {grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:2rem;} .offers {padding-block:3rem;} .about-review {padding-top:3rem;} .actions {gap:1rem;} }
</style>
